Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Short answer: usually yes — use the exact legal name that’s on your Social Security Administration (SSA) record. Whether a small spelling difference is acceptable depends on who’s asking and why, but mismatches can cause verification failures or processing delays.

What to do
- If the form asks for your "legal name" or "name as shown on Social Security card," enter the name exactly as it appears on your SSA record.  
- If you recently changed your name (marriage, divorce, court order), make sure you have updated your SSA record first — otherwise use the old name that is still on file.  
